// Knowledge (KNOWLEDGE.md): what interpretation concludes and from what, how
// features last and blur, and the shapes of what is said: what every topic's
// findings, rules and utterances are written in. A topic's own rules and
// claims are in its directory.
//
// Cut points:
// - full:     an agent perceives what happens around it.
// - reduced:  only what it takes part in: its own doings, what is done to it,
//             what is said to it (reality.tri's `reduced`).
// - abstract: as reduced.
// - frozen:   it perceives nothing; its memory's fading is reckoned from
//             times, so it is caught up as it is read.
// - code:     src/know_knowledge_*.odin: perception, recognition, memory, each
//             premise's kind, and the findings no rule concludes (#Taken,
//             #Struck, #Arrested, #Hires, #Owned, #Reserved).

// Interpretation (KNOWLEDGE.md §9): rules that derive findings from what an
// agent perceives and believes, run on what it perceives, as it perceives
// it. Each rule may need expertise: an agent less skilled than its `mastery`
// doesn't draw it, and sees only the signs. Its premises can need prior
// beliefs, too: something it saw before that is gone now.

// What a rule concludes: something about a body.
#Finding:     { about: #Body }
// Something was done to it.
#Tampered:    #Finding & {}
// Something was done to it, and hidden.
#CoveredUp:   #Finding & {}
// Something stirred there.
#Disturbance: #Finding & {}
// Someone cleaned up beside it.
#Cleaned:     #Finding & {}
// It is reserved for someone (ACTIONS.md §7), the finding's choice: what
// the agent was told.
#Reserved:    #Finding & {}
// It is someone's own, the finding's choice: as the agent was told.
#Owned:       #Finding & {}
// Someone, the finding's choice, took it from its owner: seen, or told.
#Taken:       #Finding & {}
// It (the agent itself) is under arrest, by the finding's choice.
#Arrested:    #Finding & {}
// It hires (AGENCY.md decision 15): as the agent read, or was told.
#Hires:       #Finding & {}
// It struck someone, the finding's choice (AGENCY.md §13): a threat, to
// the agent itself when it was the one struck.
#Struck:      #Finding & {}
// Someone does something the same way, again and again (AGENCY.md §8): the
// finding's choice is the way.
#Habit:       #Finding & {}
// It was swapped for another like it.
#Replaced:    #Finding & {}
// It is a forgery.
#Forged:      #Finding & {}
// It is wearing: a part that wants servicing.
#Worn:        #Finding & {}

// A rule's premises, over the body it is about.
#Premise:    {}
// a trace of this kind perceived on it now
#Sign:       #Premise & { sign: text }
// a trace of this kind perceived on it before, gone now
#Formerly:   #Premise & { formerly: text }
// a trace of this kind perceived on the floor at it or beside it
#Near:       #Premise & { near: text }
// it was seen to put things into the same container at least this often
#Repeated:   #Premise & { repeated: int }
// it was seen with more of this before, which wears on and never off, than
// it is seen with now
#Unworn:     #Premise & { unworn: text }
// a copy whose impression is not that of the seal the agent has seen of the
// issuer it claims
#Misprinted: #Premise & { misprinted: *true | false }
// it is seen worn at least this much (a part's `wear`); weighed again as
// it is seen, so a part serviced stops being so
#Wearing:    #Premise & { wearing: int }

#Skill: "painting"

// `concludes` is a #Finding type; `weight` the credence it lends, in dB. A
// `deliberate` rule takes thought: it is drawn only when the agent
// investigates (KNOWLEDGE.md §9).
#Rule: {
    premises:   [...#Premise]
    skill:      #Skill
    mastery:    int & >=0 & <=100
    concludes:  text
    weight:     int & >=0 & <=30
    deliberate: *false | true
}

// Seen putting things in the same place three times: they usually do.
usually_puts: #Rule & {
    premises:  [#Repeated & { repeated: 3 }]
    mastery:   0
    concludes: "#Habit"
    weight:    10
} @family(rules)

// How long features usually last (KNOWLEDGE.md §8, CONTENT_LANGUAGE.md §17's
// recognition): a coat changes daily, the rest of how someone looks hardly
// at all. Recognition weighs a conflict on a short-lived feature lightly: it
// may be the same one, changed.
// Something said of a feature of how things look.
#OfFeature: { feature: text }

#Persistence: #OfFeature & { persists: time }

coat_persists: #Persistence & { feature: "coat", persists: 1d } @family(persistence)

// How a feature blurs with distance (KNOWLEDGE.md §5, perception's
// precision): `blur` steps for each tile beyond arm's reach.
#Acuity: #OfFeature & { blur: int }

size_blurs: #Acuity & { feature: "size", blur: 1 } @family(acuity)

// Believed the same past `mergeAt` dB (KNOWLEDGE.md decision 13), two
// referents merge into one; a wrong merge stands until they are seen apart.
#Merging: { mergeAt: int }

identities_merge: #Merging & { mergeAt: 20 } @family(recognition)

// What agents say (KNOWLEDGE.md §10). An utterance's content is a structure,
// carried by the "said" event, and whoever is in earshot perceives it.
// Content names no referents: it describes things by kind, features, and
// where they are, and each hearer binds them to referents of its own by
// recognition.

// Every utterance is about something like `what`.
#Utterance: { what: #Body }

// An utterance about something like `what` inside `within`.
#Placing: #Utterance & { within: #Body }

// A question expects an answer from the one it is put to.
#Question: #Utterance & {}

// How the speaker says it knows (the attribution, KNOWLEDGE.md §10): it saw
// it, as sure as its memory of it is strong (in dB), or heard it, from
// someone it describes, or from no one it names.
#Source:  {}
#Saw:     #Source & { sure: int }
#Heard:   #Source & { from: #Agent }
// A promise (AGENCY.md §7): the speaker will see to it, by `when`. Hearers
// hold it as a claim about then, kept or broken as they come to find.
#Pledged: #Source & {}

// A claim, as of `when`, with how the speaker says it knows.
#Telling: #Utterance & { when: time, attribution: #Source }

// A claim naming someone like `holder`.
#Naming: #Telling & { holder: #Agent }
